afidl 1;

schema agentflow.failure.row @1;

import agentflow.semantic.core@1 as core;

// AgentFlow Static Typed Failure Row — Phase 4A.2. This module is the
// machine description of the Φ dimension of
// Computation<I, O, Φ, ε, R>: the CLOSED, NOMINAL set of typed business
// failures a computation may surface.
//
// A failure type is identified nominally: the full triple
// (SpecificationId, TypeName, pinned TypeSchemaDigest). A type enters a
// FailureRow exactly when this contract gives it a typed failure role;
// being an AFIDL schema alone makes nothing a failure. No error-message
// matching, no error codes, no exception class reflection, no
// provider-specific mapping (later Worker Failure Mapping).
//
// The six error planes are strictly separate, and only the FIRST is
// representable here:
//
//   Typed FailureValue      → Φ (this module)
//   TimedOut                → Control Outcome (SemanticIr HandleMatch)
//   Cancelled               → Control Outcome (never a Handle match)
//   RecoveryBlocked         → Recovery State (not HANDLE-catchable)
//   TaskAttemptLost         → Infrastructure Fact (never Failure<WorkerLost>)
//   RuntimeIncident         → Incident Plane (blocks progression)
//
// Φ = ∅ does NOT mean the computation succeeds: TimedOut, Cancelled,
// RecoveryBlocked, infrastructure facts and incidents all remain possible
// outside the row. Unknown failure upper bounds are expressed by a
// separate static-analysis result (Unproven), never by an empty row.
//
// This module deliberately does NOT copy the Effect Row's open/residual/
// unknown wire states: the Failure Row is a closed nominal set.
//
// Deliberately absent: FailureValue runtime payloads, TerminalOutcome,
// RuntimeIncident ABI, worker error transport, failure mapping adapters,
// ComponentContract, RecoveryContract, retry policies, journal events.
//
// This module self-hosts like the other production modules: its field
// numbering is registered as `active` rows in
// spec/registry/abi-numbers.json, and its per-type TypeSchemaDigests are
// frozen in the AFIDL corpus (case `failure-row`). No new HashV1 domain is
// introduced: type identity is TypeSchemaDigest, and no FailureRowDigest
// exists — the future ComponentContract will hash as a whole under the
// already frozen `component-contract` domain.

// One typed failure: an exact pin of a named AFIDL schema. The payload
// type is reused from the semantic core by full cross-module identity —
// never a bare string, never a redeclared reference shape. Nominal
// identity = (specification_id, type_name, schema_digest); two refs with
// the same short name under different specifications, or with different
// pinned digests, are DIFFERENT failure types and are never silently
// compatible.
record FailureTypeRef {
  1 payload_type: core.TypeSchemaRef;
}

// The closed Failure Row Φ = {F1, F2, ... Fn} of one contract: the set of
// typed business failures it may surface. Canonical order is the sorted
// nominal identity, never the source declaration order; duplicate
// declarations are rejected.
record FailureRow {
  1 failures: list<FailureTypeRef>;
}
